{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>Woe to those who decree.</b> 'Woe' is like a call against the judges and their officers and scribes:" "<b>And those who write.</b> A verb with two objects, from the heavy [binyan] with dagesh, and 'toil' is joined with 'they write':"], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {1 "Reading עמל as the word meaning 'toil/injustice,' following the context of Isaiah 10:1; the syntactic point is that עמל is the first object of the hif'il verb וּמְכַתְּבִים and כָתְבוּ is its second."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:53:07.225289258Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}